WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.866
Hello! Who are you?

2
00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:16.038
I'm a sea otter.

3
00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:20.841
Sea otters are a type of weasel.

4
00:00:20.842 --> 00:00:23.719
Where do you live?

5
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:28.519
Sea otters live in the Pacific Ocean.

6
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:33.224
We live in North America and Asia.

7
00:00:33.225 --> 00:00:38.052
Do you ever go on land?

8
00:00:38.053 --> 00:00:42.395
Sea otters go on land to rest sometimes.

9
00:00:42.396 --> 00:00:48.278
But we mostly stay in the water.

10
00:00:48.279 --> 00:00:58.215
We even sleep in the water.

11
00:00:58.216 --> 00:01:03.708
How do you do that?

12
00:01:03.709 --> 00:01:07.707
We float on our backs.

13
00:01:07.708 --> 00:01:12.204
Sometimes we sleep wrapped in kelp.

14
00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:16.597
The kelp keeps us from drifting away.

15
00:01:16.598 --> 00:01:19.741
What do you eat?

16
00:01:19.742 --> 00:01:24.246
Sea otters eat fish and octopuses.

17
00:01:24.247 --> 00:01:28.819
We also like crabs and clams.

18
00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.825
We use rocks to break them open.

19
00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:40.244
Your fur looks thick!

20
00:01:40.245 --> 00:01:44.379
Our fur is very thick.

21
00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:48.382
It's also waterproof.

22
00:01:48.383 --> 00:01:53.582
Our fur keeps us warm and dry.

23
00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:58.057
Do you have any enemies?

24
00:01:58.058 --> 00:02:04.983
Killer whales and sharks sometimes eat us.

25
00:02:04.984 --> 00:02:11.383
Our webbed feet help us swim away fast.

26
00:02:11.384 --> 00:02:15.091
I'll see you later.

27
00:02:15.092 --> 00:02:19.778
I need to clean my fur now.

28
00:02:19.779 --> 00:02:27.745
Good-bye, Sea Otter!

